    windows_msvc_stage2_rejected_struct_receiver_route_threads_2026-09-01, 2, "2026-11-03 stale check (conc): not a concurrency race despite the filename. The rejection was the Stage-3 positional route failing with `Error: --threads requires a positive integer` (src/app/io/_CliCompile/native_build.spl:511, compile_targets.spl:960) while check-bootstrap-stage2-struct-receiver.shs passes `--threads 1` (:78, :152). Linux Stage 2 on release/1.0.0 has since been ADMITTED (b56c3e203ff, 2026-10-24) with the same probe passing. No Windows MSVC re-run is recorded after 2026-09-01 and the MSVC lane is optional per CLAUDE.md, so the Windows-specific cause (stale frozen stage2 arg parser vs current source) is unverified. Kept open; needs an MSVC Stage 2 re-run on a Windows host."
    windows_msvc_stage2_rejected_struct_receiver_route_threads_2026-09-01, 3, "2026-11-04 bootstrap triage: CLOSED obsolete. MSVC lane dropped by policy (Windows = llvm-mingw UCRT only, NO MSVC; CLAUDE.md Critical Rules)."

